WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.100
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.105 --> 00:01.105
MkvDrama.net

3
01:01.665 --> 01:06.385
Taming The Husband

4
01:06.505 --> 01:09.025
Episode 8

5
01:11.025 --> 01:12.905
What are you doing? Get out!

6
01:13.185 --> 01:14.985
Where are your manners? I'm your sister-in-law!

7
01:15.065 --> 01:17.305
You wish! You're vile, shameless, and disgusting!

8
01:17.385 --> 01:18.545
You call yourself my sister-in-law?

9
01:18.625 --> 01:20.145
-Someone-- -Shut up!

10
01:21.625 --> 01:22.705
Baozhu,

11
01:23.225 --> 01:24.225
Just in time.

12
01:24.305 --> 01:26.545
Didn't you want me to find someone to practice on? I've found someone.

13
01:29.385 --> 01:30.625
It's too late to change your mind.

14
01:31.425 --> 01:32.985
You're in this with me now.

15
01:33.065 --> 01:34.185
Just teach me.

16
01:36.665 --> 01:37.825
Understand?

17
01:42.025 --> 01:43.665
Our whole family has searched for a cure.

18
01:43.985 --> 01:45.465
Those great doctors and healers failed,

19
01:45.585 --> 01:48.465
but he can? Do you take me for a three-year-old?

20
01:48.745 --> 01:50.945
I'd heard your condition was beyond treatment.

21
01:51.305 --> 01:52.825
When I took your pulse the other night,

22
01:52.905 --> 01:54.265
I felt a faint sign of strength.

23
01:54.345 --> 01:55.865
There's still hope of recovery.

24
01:56.225 --> 01:58.545
You're nothing but a dog kept by my uncle's family.

25
01:58.865 --> 02:00.225
We don't even feed you.

26
02:00.385 --> 02:02.145
How could I trust you to guard my door?

27
02:03.065 --> 02:04.305
We each get what we need.

28
02:04.505 --> 02:05.985
Lady Jin promised me something in return.

29
02:06.465 --> 02:07.665
What?

30
02:09.625 --> 02:11.305
A letter recommending him for the medical exam in the capital.

31
02:11.745 --> 02:12.985
Your letter alone is no use.

32
02:13.065 --> 02:14.745
It needs Grandmother's seal.

33
02:14.825 --> 02:17.825
I know. But if he cures Yan's legs,

34
02:17.905 --> 02:19.025
would Grandmother refuse?

35
02:24.065 --> 02:25.265
You'd better not try anything.

36
02:25.345 --> 02:27.225
You talk too much.

37
02:29.585 --> 02:30.585
Hold still.

38
02:30.665 --> 02:31.665
Look.

39
02:31.745 --> 02:32.745
Like this.

40
02:32.825 --> 02:33.945
Just as I told you last time, follow the meridians.

41
02:34.025 --> 02:35.345
Along the meridians.

42
02:38.745 --> 02:40.305
Why can't I feel that pulse now?

43
02:40.825 --> 02:42.105
What else did you do that day?

44
02:43.025 --> 02:46.065
That day, I was beaten, too.

45
02:46.225 --> 02:48.945
Anything else? Was anything different from usual?

46
02:50.745 --> 02:56.865
No. You can go.

47
03:08.785 --> 03:10.025
I didn't use the medicine that day.

48
03:14.545 --> 03:16.825
Who gave you this medicine? How long have you been using it?

49
03:17.505 --> 03:18.825
Someone from the second branch.

50
03:19.865 --> 03:21.265
Lady Qin found the prescription.

51
03:22.145 --> 03:23.545
Grandmother even praised her for it.

52
03:24.585 --> 03:26.505
Could they be trying to poison you?

53
03:27.065 --> 03:29.985
Come on! Let's go to Grandmother right now and report them!

54
03:30.065 --> 03:32.425
Wait. Think before you act.

55
03:33.225 --> 03:34.585
If there were something wrong with it,

56
03:35.265 --> 03:37.505
why didn't our doctors and healers notice?

57
03:37.585 --> 03:40.305
But… What if they were paid off?

58
03:40.385 --> 03:42.625
Or afraid of getting involved, so they kept their mouths shut?

59
03:42.945 --> 03:44.065
Let's go. Let's go.

60
03:44.905 --> 03:46.425
Not everyone is a coward.

61
03:47.385 --> 03:48.425
However foolish they are,

62
03:49.345 --> 03:50.945
surely they wouldn't go that far.

63
03:53.985 --> 03:55.065
You should go.

64
04:01.065 --> 04:03.225
Listen to me. Listen to me.

65
04:04.225 --> 04:05.385
Once your legs are better,

66
04:05.585 --> 04:07.705
I'll show you off at the shipping festival.

67
04:07.785 --> 04:08.945
Just think how grand we'd look!

68
04:09.665 --> 04:10.705
Don't forget,

69
04:11.745 --> 04:13.265
you haven't finished your lessons.

70
04:15.625 --> 04:18.105
How about this? Stop using the medicine for a while,

71
04:18.265 --> 04:19.425
and I'll massage your legs again.

72
04:19.625 --> 04:20.985
What if there's a chance?

73
04:21.625 --> 04:22.625
Once your legs are better,

74
04:22.745 --> 04:24.505
we can expose them then.

75
04:26.985 --> 04:28.505
What chance could I possibly have?

76
04:29.825 --> 04:31.065
There is one.

77
04:43.025 --> 04:45.225
This is moxa. The Compendium of Materia Medica says:

78
04:45.505 --> 04:47.265
"Mugwort is bitter and pungent, warm when raw, hot when processed."

79
04:47.345 --> 04:49.065
"It is purely yang and nontoxic."

80
04:50.545 --> 04:52.585
If there's nothing wrong with it, give it back to Yan.

81
04:52.745 --> 04:53.905
You keep making a fuss over nothing.

82
04:53.985 --> 04:54.985
I almost believed you!

83
04:56.185 --> 04:57.345
If the medicine's fine,

84
04:57.505 --> 04:59.385
why aren't Yan's legs getting any better?

85
04:59.465 --> 05:01.185
He must stop using it, whatever it is.

86
05:01.265 --> 05:04.065
What's wrong with it? Anyone can talk.

87
05:04.145 --> 05:05.945
If you're so capable, get him on his feet!

88
05:07.905 --> 05:09.025
You're right, young master.

89
05:09.425 --> 05:10.705
If I were that capable,

90
05:11.305 --> 05:12.545
I wouldn't be living off someone else.

91
05:13.105 --> 05:14.865
Unless we try, how will we know?

92
05:15.425 --> 05:17.625
Just as you fail time and again, yet keep trying.

93
05:17.905 --> 05:19.665
If you can do it, why can't anyone else?

94
05:20.225 --> 05:21.785
Isn't that rather unfair?

95
05:35.105 --> 05:37.425
Lady Jin, what is the meaning of this?

96
05:39.905 --> 05:42.385
Before, I didn't apply myself to my lessons.

97
05:43.185 --> 05:45.385
My rashness got me confined by my lady,

98
05:45.865 --> 05:47.145
and by breaking the rules,

99
05:48.265 --> 05:49.745
I got my husband punished, too.

100
05:50.105 --> 05:51.145
I feel ashamed.

101
05:51.425 --> 05:52.745
I want to make amends.

102
05:53.385 --> 05:55.145
I spent all night embroidering this.

103
05:55.225 --> 05:56.465
I know it isn't pretty,

104
05:56.665 --> 05:57.985
but I've done my best.

105
05:58.505 --> 05:59.865
Please teach me, Matron Fang.

106
06:04.105 --> 06:06.465
Swallows are the hardest to embroider.

107
06:06.745 --> 06:08.065
Their colors are rich,

108
06:08.345 --> 06:10.265
but their movements are light.

109
06:10.825 --> 06:12.745
The stitches must be close, never stiff,

110
06:12.985 --> 06:14.105
loose, but never untidy.

111
06:15.265 --> 06:17.305
I'm not skilled enough.

112
06:17.825 --> 06:19.465
Find yourself a better teacher.

113
06:19.545 --> 06:22.385
Matron Fang, Madam promised me

114
06:22.785 --> 06:24.305
that once I'd completed your lessons,

115
06:24.425 --> 06:26.665
my husband and I could go to the shipping festival.

116
06:27.425 --> 06:28.505
It's not just for myself.

117
06:28.785 --> 06:30.065
I want to bring honor to the Xies.

118
06:30.505 --> 06:31.625
She said

119
06:31.705 --> 06:33.225
your embroidery's poor, and she won't teach you.

120
06:33.305 --> 06:34.865
What's the point of pestering her?

121
06:35.385 --> 06:37.385
Look, Matron Fang. I embroidered this.

122
06:38.705 --> 06:39.945
You're right, Miss Xi.

123
06:40.305 --> 06:42.105
I'm too impatient, unlike you.

124
06:42.505 --> 06:43.865
I still have much to learn.

125
06:44.025 --> 06:45.385
But things change so quickly.

126
06:45.465 --> 06:46.905
How can we know unless we try?

127
06:47.185 --> 06:48.265
Just like you,

128
06:48.385 --> 06:49.945
you fail time and again, yet keep trying.

129
06:50.265 --> 06:51.705
If you can do it, why can't anyone else?

130
06:52.105 --> 06:53.265
Isn't that rather unfair?

131
06:55.505 --> 06:56.905
Jin Baozhu! You--

132
06:57.865 --> 06:58.945
A lady keeps her composure.

133
06:59.385 --> 07:00.985
Please remember that, Miss Xi.

134
07:02.145 --> 07:03.225
Go back now.

135
07:05.425 --> 07:06.545
Yes.

136
07:12.025 --> 07:13.025
Please teach me.

137
07:13.505 --> 07:14.985
You're a hopeless block of wood,

138
07:15.505 --> 07:17.705
but at least you know to keep asking.

139
07:18.745 --> 07:19.785
Come in.

140
07:20.305 --> 07:23.105
Let's see if I can carve you into shape.

141
08:01.385 --> 08:02.465
Like this.

142
08:19.425 --> 08:21.145
It's not that cold. Leave it open.

143
08:26.025 --> 08:27.065
Once winter's over,

144
08:27.505 --> 08:28.785
spring won't be far behind.

145
08:43.145 --> 08:44.305
What are you up to now?

146
08:44.745 --> 08:46.225
Always running off somewhere.

147
08:47.145 --> 08:48.305
I'm learning my manners,

148
08:48.505 --> 08:49.745
so I can show off properly.

149
08:50.105 --> 08:51.665
Lessons that keep you out past midnight?

150
09:09.665 --> 09:11.785
Jin Baozhu! Who's this man you've brought home?

151
09:17.305 --> 09:20.105
Jin Baozhu! Who's this man you've brought home?

152
09:26.825 --> 09:28.785
Where did this come from?

153
09:29.305 --> 09:30.625
The tree they cut down in the courtyard.

154
09:31.025 --> 09:32.025
What did you make it for?

155
09:34.265 --> 09:35.545
Because I wanted to.

156
09:36.065 --> 09:37.225
Go on. Go.

157
09:43.665 --> 09:44.745
You…

158
09:48.865 --> 09:50.225
I already told you

159
09:50.345 --> 09:51.465
not to waste your time.

160
09:52.905 --> 09:54.345
Why won't you listen?

161
09:54.785 --> 09:56.265
Besides, what sort of person

162
09:56.345 --> 09:57.505
keeps this thing in their room?

163
09:58.425 --> 09:59.985
Won't it give you nightmares?

164
10:00.545 --> 10:01.585
Throw it out.

165
10:01.665 --> 10:02.665
I'm not afraid.

166
10:03.265 --> 10:04.585
I'm afraid your legs won't get better.

167
10:10.505 --> 10:11.745
I will say it!

168
10:12.385 --> 10:14.105
A wound heals faster in the open.

169
10:14.225 --> 10:15.705
You can't cover it up forever

170
10:15.785 --> 10:16.905
and let it rot inside.

171
10:33.585 --> 10:34.705
That's not what I meant.

172
10:34.825 --> 10:35.985
I know.

173
10:37.185 --> 10:38.825
But there are things

174
10:39.945 --> 10:41.065
you don't know.

175
10:56.185 --> 10:57.305
Here.

176
11:16.425 --> 11:18.225
How could falling from a horse leave you so badly hurt?

177
11:19.305 --> 11:20.465
Here, on my calf,

178
11:22.305 --> 11:24.425
iron shackles cut deep into the flesh.

179
11:25.345 --> 11:26.825
Once they were taken off,

180
11:27.145 --> 11:28.825
they left this deep groove.

181
11:33.665 --> 11:34.785
And here, my knee.

182
11:36.705 --> 11:39.185
They smashed the kneecap.

183
11:41.825 --> 11:42.865
It can never heal.

184
11:48.385 --> 11:49.545
On my thigh,

185
11:51.305 --> 11:53.185
a branding iron was pressed deep.

186
11:53.985 --> 11:55.545
Scabs crowded together,

187
11:55.905 --> 11:57.065
layer upon layer.

188
11:58.505 --> 12:00.065
You don't know.

189
12:01.425 --> 12:02.985
But I do.

190
12:04.865 --> 12:07.025
I know they're hideous enough to turn your stomach.

191
12:07.905 --> 12:08.985
I know...

192
12:10.945 --> 12:12.545
you'll run when you see them.

193
12:17.625 --> 12:18.745
Frightened?

194
12:25.025 --> 12:26.185
Then leave.

195
12:50.705 --> 12:51.865
You don't know.

196
12:52.985 --> 12:54.385
You don't know that I'll stay,

197
12:55.185 --> 12:57.505
You don't know that I'll hold your hand.

198
12:58.865 --> 13:00.425
And you don't know that one day,

199
13:00.945 --> 13:02.185
I'll heal your legs.

200
13:03.625 --> 13:04.905
But I do.

201
13:05.705 --> 13:06.945
Xie Yan,

202
13:07.745 --> 13:08.745
I've known you

203
13:09.585 --> 13:11.225
far longer than you realize.

204
13:13.265 --> 13:15.785
Even a great scholar

205
13:16.225 --> 13:17.665
can't know everything.

206
13:19.625 --> 13:20.745
Aren't you afraid?

207
13:21.865 --> 13:23.025
No.

208
13:23.825 --> 13:24.865
But I am.

209
13:28.825 --> 13:29.985
Things have changed.

210
13:31.465 --> 13:32.945
I'm no longer

211
13:34.665 --> 13:36.705
the Xie Yan who rode through the streets.

212
13:38.825 --> 13:39.905
Things have changed.

213
13:40.665 --> 13:42.865
My embroidered swallows are quite good now.

214
13:52.945 --> 13:54.545
Yet you still don't believe in me.

215
14:16.585 --> 14:17.985
I gave you a chance.

216
14:19.825 --> 14:21.865
You walked into my trap yourself.

217
14:34.625 --> 14:36.265
You called us here to see this?

218
14:37.145 --> 14:39.065
You're so fond of Yan. You can have it.

219
14:39.145 --> 14:40.465
Cuddle it in bed at night.

220
14:40.545 --> 14:42.505
You're mad! I don't want it!

221
14:42.865 --> 14:45.025
Besides, didn't you need someone to practice on?

222
14:45.985 --> 14:47.745
I've found someone better suited.

223
14:53.825 --> 14:55.545
-My lord. -Yan.

224
14:56.425 --> 14:58.025
I know about the letter.

225
14:58.585 --> 14:59.745
Thank you for doing this.

226
15:00.065 --> 15:01.185
Thank you.

227
15:12.265 --> 15:13.865
Your pulse is sluggish and hard as stone.

228
15:15.105 --> 15:16.345
Qi and blood can't reach your legs.

229
15:17.625 --> 15:18.625
How strange.

230
15:20.225 --> 15:21.825
All those doctors and healers

231
15:22.785 --> 15:24.105
said just the same.

232
15:40.145 --> 15:41.185
Benzoin.

233
15:42.745 --> 15:44.545
That's the root of your trouble.

234
15:45.825 --> 15:47.105
What nonsense are you talking?

235
15:47.345 --> 15:49.025
My mother prepared that benzoin especially for him.

236
15:50.465 --> 15:52.065
Benzoin revives the senses.

237
15:52.745 --> 15:56.145
Moxa warms and opens the meridians, dispels cold, and eases pain.

238
15:56.465 --> 15:58.425
Used separately, both are good medicines.

239
15:59.505 --> 16:01.625
But together, it's a different matter entirely.

240
16:01.905 --> 16:03.305
Benzoin spreads rapidly through the body.

241
16:03.385 --> 16:04.625
Moxa is warming and potent.

242
16:04.865 --> 16:07.145
The two together are like pouring oil on a fire.

243
16:07.505 --> 16:09.585
At first, inhaling it brings relief throughout the body.

244
16:09.665 --> 16:10.905
Over time, they deplete the blood and body fluids,

245
16:10.985 --> 16:11.985
causing chronic illness.

246
16:12.705 --> 16:14.945
How long have you used it?

247
16:15.105 --> 16:16.225
Have you used it continuously?

248
16:17.505 --> 16:18.665
Ever since I fell ill.

249
16:18.865 --> 16:19.905
Once in the morning, once at night,

250
16:20.865 --> 16:22.265
and again in damp or rainy weather.

251
16:22.625 --> 16:24.425
Except for the night you took my pulse,

252
16:24.785 --> 16:26.225
I've never missed a dose.

253
16:26.425 --> 16:29.145
That explains it. It may calm you and ease the pain,

254
16:29.225 --> 16:30.265
but it's addictive.

255
16:30.945 --> 16:32.745
The meridians in your legs are severely blocked.

256
16:33.105 --> 16:35.585
Ordinary massage probably won't help.

257
16:36.025 --> 16:37.425
First, moxibustion to open the meridians,

258
16:37.665 --> 16:38.865
together with acupressure.

259
16:39.265 --> 16:40.425
Then we can make gradual progress.

260
16:41.185 --> 16:44.625
But there's one difficult thing to do first.

261
16:48.185 --> 16:49.385
If you're giving up the medicine,

262
16:50.265 --> 16:51.545
all of this has to go.

263
16:59.705 --> 17:00.785
Why are you looking at me?

264
17:01.025 --> 17:03.265
If you weren't looking at me, how would you know?

265
17:12.785 --> 17:13.905
Later tonight…

266
17:17.305 --> 17:18.385
Once the lights are out…

267
17:23.225 --> 17:24.425
It's all right.

268
18:36.945 --> 18:37.985
Ask Jianwei to fetch some.

269
18:38.665 --> 18:39.705
Just a little will do.

270
18:40.065 --> 18:41.745
Hold on. Just a little longer.

271
18:49.185 --> 18:51.425
I want some soup.

272
18:52.625 --> 18:55.385
Jianwei, ask the kitchen to make some soup.

273
18:55.465 --> 18:57.025
Yingtao, get a fresh basin of water.

274
18:57.265 --> 18:58.265
-Yes. -This month's private allowance

275
18:58.345 --> 18:59.345
has all gone on medicine.

276
18:59.425 --> 19:00.585
It's not mealtime.

277
19:00.665 --> 19:01.745
They won't give us anything.

278
19:04.865 --> 19:05.985
I'll go and ask.

279
19:07.025 --> 19:08.025
Watch him.

280
19:08.105 --> 19:09.625
Shut the doors and windows before it rains.

281
19:09.705 --> 19:10.865
Yes.

282
19:12.225 --> 19:13.505
My lord.

283
19:13.785 --> 19:15.025
My lord, hold on!

284
19:16.505 --> 19:18.025
My lord! My lord.

285
19:30.865 --> 19:31.865
My lady. My lady, I…

286
19:32.025 --> 19:33.745
-Why have you come out? -My lord's asleep.

287
19:33.945 --> 19:35.225
Let me carry that, my lady.

288
19:37.985 --> 19:39.585
My lady! My lady!

289
19:40.465 --> 19:41.625
Xie Yan!

290
19:51.345 --> 19:53.105
Do you know, just to get what you asked for,

291
19:53.185 --> 19:54.385
how long I had to beg?

292
19:55.025 --> 19:56.345
You only wanted me out of the way

293
19:56.425 --> 19:58.305
so you could do this! You…

294
20:06.185 --> 20:07.305
You fool!

295
20:08.145 --> 20:09.705
All you say is to bear it.

296
20:10.865 --> 20:12.225
All of you tell me to bear it!

297
20:12.545 --> 20:13.705
It's not your face being slapped,

298
20:13.785 --> 20:14.945
so you don't feel the pain!

299
20:23.705 --> 20:24.825
Don't blame him, my lady.

300
20:25.065 --> 20:27.305
It was me. He couldn't bear it anymore,

301
20:27.385 --> 20:28.665
so I gave him an empty pipe.

302
20:29.665 --> 20:31.505
He didn't want you to see him like this.

303
20:32.225 --> 20:33.585
That's why he sent you away.

304
20:37.185 --> 20:39.945
I… I hate you, Jin Baozhu!

305
20:43.825 --> 20:44.985
Go away!

306
21:18.985 --> 21:20.025
I'm sorry.

307
21:22.585 --> 21:23.625
I'm sorry.

308
21:23.905 --> 21:25.265
Hate me, then.

309
21:26.065 --> 21:27.465
I'm not leaving.

310
21:28.185 --> 21:29.945
Even if you hate me, I'm staying.

311
21:30.305 --> 21:31.505
I want you to stand,

312
21:31.945 --> 21:33.265
taller than anyone.

313
22:08.465 --> 22:10.425
Lady Jin really cares about your master.

314
22:11.065 --> 22:13.025
She came through the rain to fetch me.

315
22:15.025 --> 22:17.185
I don't think I'm needed now.

316
22:18.305 --> 22:20.785
May I ask when my lord will recover?

317
22:22.905 --> 22:24.665
His legs can already move.

318
22:25.185 --> 22:26.745
But he's under too much mental strain.

319
22:27.545 --> 22:28.905
He needs to keep practicing.

320
22:42.065 --> 22:43.345
I can't even stand steadily.

321
22:43.825 --> 22:45.065
How am I supposed to practice?

322
22:45.625 --> 22:47.025
Close your eyes first.

323
23:07.345 --> 23:08.705
Practice in your mind.

324
23:08.985 --> 23:10.225
In my mind?

325
23:11.385 --> 23:13.625
Imagine this. Every day,

326
23:13.785 --> 23:15.865
you work hard butchering pigs and selling meat.

327
23:16.145 --> 23:19.665
Then, suddenly, a thug snatches your purse.

328
23:20.305 --> 23:21.625
You're furious,

329
23:21.705 --> 23:22.985
but you're so tired.

330
23:23.065 --> 23:24.345
Still, you have to chase him.

331
23:24.425 --> 23:27.145
So you lift your left foot,

332
23:27.585 --> 23:28.945
then your right.

333
23:29.345 --> 23:30.585
Left foot, right foot.

334
23:31.185 --> 23:33.025
Left foot, right foot.

335
23:33.585 --> 23:35.305
Left, right.

336
23:35.865 --> 23:39.385
Left, right. Left, right. Left, right.

337
23:39.465 --> 23:41.425
Walk faster and faster. Faster and faster.

338
23:41.505 --> 23:42.665
Run faster and faster. Faster and faster.

339
23:43.185 --> 23:45.145
At last, you catch up with him.

340
23:45.225 --> 23:46.705
He swings a punch at you,

341
23:46.785 --> 23:49.225
so you dodge quickly, left and right,

342
23:49.545 --> 23:52.025
with quick little steps, until you've dodged the blow.

343
23:52.425 --> 23:54.105
You plant your feet, lift your leg,

344
23:54.305 --> 23:56.225
and launch a flying kick. You kick him away.

345
23:56.945 --> 23:57.985
Congratulations!

346
23:58.945 --> 24:00.385
You've got your purse back.

347
24:07.105 --> 24:09.065
Ridiculous. Are we playing house?

348
24:09.145 --> 24:10.265
What do you know?

349
24:10.745 --> 24:12.025
There's a method to this.

350
24:12.265 --> 24:13.585
Whether I strike the front or back,

351
24:13.665 --> 24:15.465
hard, slowly, or not at all,

352
24:15.665 --> 24:17.025
each tells you to lift your leg,

353
24:17.105 --> 24:18.305
move, or hold still.

354
24:18.385 --> 24:20.305
Every day, listen to the drumbeats

355
24:20.465 --> 24:21.465
and practice in your mind.

356
24:21.785 --> 24:22.905
Think it through, day and night.

357
24:22.985 --> 24:24.225
Once your mind finds its way,

358
24:24.305 --> 24:26.625
your legs will follow. Well?

359
24:28.385 --> 24:29.745
Let's try again.

360
24:31.065 --> 24:33.065
Have you got another story?

361
24:33.145 --> 24:35.225
Of course. Besides chasing thugs,

362
24:35.305 --> 24:36.905
there's chasing ruffians,

363
24:37.105 --> 24:39.625
carts, or wild dogs. What would you like to chase?

364
24:53.145 --> 24:54.225
Serve the tea.

365
25:28.465 --> 25:32.425
Smooth, with a lingering sweetness.

366
25:33.785 --> 25:37.265
Very good. You're really getting the hang of it.

367
25:38.345 --> 25:40.145
What brings you here?

368
25:40.985 --> 25:43.945
You said that once I'd learned my manners,

369
25:44.025 --> 25:45.545
I could go to the shipping festival.

370
25:46.345 --> 25:48.665
Does that still stand?

371
25:57.865 --> 25:59.065
Grain Transport Wharf The Bai family

372
26:02.105 --> 26:03.465
So that's what you're after?

373
26:03.545 --> 26:04.545
Yes.

374
26:04.625 --> 26:06.425
Move aside! Move aside!

375
26:07.105 --> 26:08.425
-Who's that? -My master has a contest to get to!

376
26:08.585 --> 26:10.145
Move! Out of the way!

377
26:10.225 --> 26:11.225
Really?

378
26:11.425 --> 26:12.505
Move!

379
26:13.145 --> 26:14.425
This way, my lord.

380
26:19.625 --> 26:20.665
It's all right.

381
26:20.745 --> 26:22.225
Who's that? Who tripped me?

382
26:25.385 --> 26:26.385
This…

383
26:26.465 --> 26:30.545
Chengjiang, how have you been?

384
26:36.265 --> 26:37.945
Master Bai. Master Huang.

385
26:38.345 --> 26:39.385
It's been a while.

386
26:50.305 --> 26:53.865
Junmei, that trip just now seemed rather suspicious.

387
26:54.425 --> 26:55.425
Can you prove it?

388
26:57.545 --> 26:58.945
Unless you're sure you can win,

389
26:59.145 --> 27:00.825
you shouldn't pick a fight.

390
27:01.185 --> 27:03.625
Besides, if a dog bites you,

391
27:04.185 --> 27:05.625
do you bite it back?

392
27:05.705 --> 27:06.825
Huang Yulan The Huang family's eldest legitimate son

393
27:11.265 --> 27:12.825
Why haven't the ladies of your house

394
27:12.905 --> 27:14.265
joined us today?

395
27:15.945 --> 27:17.065
Please, have some.

396
27:17.665 --> 27:19.465
The shops are packed at festival time.

397
27:19.585 --> 27:21.385
They've all gone to help out there,

398
27:21.465 --> 27:22.625
and can't get away.

399
27:27.345 --> 27:29.865
Nangong's Five Talents

400
27:30.145 --> 27:31.785
It's a promise. Don't forget!

401
27:32.145 --> 27:33.865
Mother.

402
27:34.105 --> 27:36.705
Let the ceremony begin!

403
27:36.825 --> 27:38.665
Grain Transport Wharf

404
27:59.185 --> 28:02.105
Today, at the shipping festival,

405
28:02.585 --> 28:06.065
the whole city has gathered.

406
28:06.145 --> 28:09.225
I join the people of this prefecture

407
28:09.305 --> 28:11.185
in celebrating together.

408
28:11.505 --> 28:14.065
There will be three contests.

409
28:14.505 --> 28:17.505
Each of Yangzhou's four great families in grain transport

410
28:17.585 --> 28:21.345
shall send four representatives to compete.

411
28:21.625 --> 28:24.185
The lowest-scoring family is eliminated each round.

412
28:24.305 --> 28:25.945
The last family standing

413
28:26.025 --> 28:28.465
will be this year's champion.

414
28:28.785 --> 28:30.265
This year, in the Huaiyang Circuit,

415
28:30.345 --> 28:31.865
the largest shipping contract

416
28:31.945 --> 28:35.105
will go entirely to the winning family.

417
28:38.105 --> 28:41.385
Let the contest begin!

418
28:41.465 --> 28:42.905
Grain Transport Wharf

419
28:43.705 --> 28:45.185
Those two, one's a Huang, one's a Bai.

420
28:45.265 --> 28:46.465
How are they on the same team?

421
28:47.745 --> 28:49.345
They're cousins, after a fashion.

422
28:50.945 --> 28:52.705
One sailor is at the mainmast,

423
28:52.785 --> 28:54.025
flying a blue flag.

424
28:54.305 --> 28:57.505
Another hangs a white flag at an angle on the secondary mast.

425
28:57.785 --> 28:59.265
One sailor stands at the bow,

426
28:59.345 --> 29:01.945
fingers together, hand at chest height,

427
29:02.025 --> 29:03.265
palm facing down,

428
29:03.345 --> 29:04.825
and presses down three times.

429
29:05.185 --> 29:07.265
What does it mean?

430
29:10.785 --> 29:13.185
That's easy. Our convoy proceeds as normal.

431
29:13.265 --> 29:14.825
The first three ships slow down in stages.

432
29:14.905 --> 29:16.865
Close up the rear. No overtaking.

433
29:19.865 --> 29:21.145
The Xie family The Bai family

434
29:21.265 --> 29:22.625
A sailor at the mainmast

435
29:22.705 --> 29:24.905
raises a red flag bearing a black blade.

436
29:25.345 --> 29:27.945
Another waves a yellow flag at the bow

437
29:28.025 --> 29:29.425
in wide sweeps.

438
29:30.105 --> 29:31.505
The orders conflict.

439
29:31.585 --> 29:33.625
Which takes priority?

440
29:33.745 --> 29:35.985
Enemy ahead! All hands fight!

441
29:36.265 --> 29:37.425
First, form up to repel the pirates,

442
29:37.585 --> 29:38.825
then save the ship.

443
29:39.545 --> 29:41.105
A sailor at the bow

444
29:41.185 --> 29:43.265
strikes a small gong hard three times.

445
29:43.345 --> 29:46.025
Close ranks? Pass through a lock?

446
29:46.225 --> 29:47.865
Or give way?

447
29:50.225 --> 29:52.105
Fog ahead. Close ranks. Stay within earshot of nearby ships.

448
29:52.305 --> 29:53.345
Take great care.

449
29:53.425 --> 29:55.385
Grain Transport Wharf

450
29:55.625 --> 29:57.065
Xie family, 12 points.

451
29:57.145 --> 29:58.545
Bai family, 10 points.

452
29:58.625 --> 29:59.865
Su family, seven points.

453
29:59.945 --> 30:01.265
Yang family, six points.

454
30:01.385 --> 30:02.745
The Yang family is eliminated.

455
30:02.825 --> 30:05.025
Good! Good! Good!

456
30:05.385 --> 30:06.425
Good!

457
30:07.065 --> 30:08.145
Good!

458
30:08.305 --> 30:11.345
Load the hold. Stack and tie the grain.

459
30:11.425 --> 30:12.865
This round is Loading the Hold.

460
30:13.625 --> 30:16.825
Your allotted area is your grain ship.

461
30:16.905 --> 30:18.425
Before this incense stick burns out,

462
30:18.625 --> 30:19.785
load your grain.

463
30:20.265 --> 30:21.865
When the incense runs out,

464
30:22.145 --> 30:25.705
the ship with the least grain is out.

465
30:31.225 --> 30:32.345
Out of my way!

466
30:45.385 --> 30:46.745
Have you heard the saying,

467
30:46.905 --> 30:49.265
"When two fight, a third takes the prize"?

468
30:49.345 --> 30:50.345
Then have you heard how

469
30:50.425 --> 30:52.665
Tian Ji won a horse race by giving up a little to win big?

470
30:55.625 --> 30:56.865
What race? On a farm?

471
30:57.625 --> 30:59.025
Tian Ji's horse race.

472
30:59.585 --> 31:01.585
Send your worst horse against their best,

473
31:01.665 --> 31:03.665
your best against their middle horse,

474
31:03.745 --> 31:05.625
and your middle horse against their worst.

475
31:05.945 --> 31:07.585
Let weaker horses face stronger ones, and stronger horses beat weaker ones.

476
31:07.665 --> 31:09.265
Give up a battle to win the war,

477
31:09.345 --> 31:10.585
and turn defeat into victory.

478
31:11.065 --> 31:12.345
Heng is very capable,

479
31:12.585 --> 31:15.425
but his old illness has flared up.

480
31:15.625 --> 31:16.665
I'm all right.

481
31:20.065 --> 31:21.985
Madam, let me take Heng's place.

482
31:22.065 --> 31:23.705
No. My son can win this.

483
31:23.945 --> 31:25.305
What do we need you for?

484
31:25.745 --> 31:27.785
Heng can't hold on much longer.

485
31:30.625 --> 31:32.385
-Perhaps… -Mother! Mother!

486
31:32.465 --> 31:33.945
Think carefully about this.

487
31:34.025 --> 31:36.465
I believe my son can win, so he will!

488
31:36.745 --> 31:38.825
All the families are here today.

489
31:39.265 --> 31:40.825
If we replace him halfway through,

490
31:40.905 --> 31:43.305
then… what would they think of Heng?

491
31:43.385 --> 31:44.425
Don't you agree, Mother?

492
31:44.505 --> 31:46.625
The Bais are playing such dirty tricks.

493
31:46.705 --> 31:47.865
What have we got to be afraid of?

494
31:48.625 --> 31:50.865
Madam, please let me go!

495
31:50.945 --> 31:52.105
I've learned my manners.

496
31:52.185 --> 31:53.705
I won't disgrace the family.

497
31:54.745 --> 31:56.065
I promise.

498
31:56.065 --> 31:57.065
MkvDrama.net
